.TH "LMM" "1" "Nov 2026" "lmm 2.3.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
lmm-profile-fill - Install a collection profile's pending mods from downloaded archives


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm profile fill <profile> [dir-or-archive...] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Install the pending mods of a profile imported from a NexusMods collection
from archives you downloaded yourself.

.PP
A free NexusMods account is not served downloads through the API, so a
collection import saves the profile with every mod pending. Download each
file from its page (the import lists them), then point this command at the
folder you saved them to - usually ~/Downloads. Each archive is matched to
a pending mod by the size and md5 checksum the collection records for its
file, and the matches are installed as if downloaded: with the installer
(FOMOD) choices and mod type the collection records, and, for a mod the
curator wants on its newest file, set to update automatically.

.PP
With no folder named, it looks in your downloads folder ($XDG_DOWNLOAD_DIR,
else the one your desktop's user-dirs names, else ~/Downloads).

.PP
Only the folder's top level is read and links in it are never followed; a
link named on the command line is refused too, unless it is the folder
itself. A file is read only when its size is a pending file's. Your files
are copied, never moved or deleted. Run it again as you download more: each
run installs what it finds and says what is still pending.

.PP
Examples:
  lmm profile fill "Essential Mods" --game skyrim-se
  lmm profile fill "Essential Mods" ~/Downloads --game skyrim-se
  lmm profile fill "Essential Mods" ~/Downloads/skse64_2_02_06.7z --game skyrim-se
  lmm profile fill "Essential Mods" ~/Downloads --game skyrim-se --dry-run


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	print what the fill would install without changing anything

.PP
\fB--fomod-choices\fP=""
	answer FOMOD installer questions from a JSON file (the profile's fomod: shape or Vortex's choices array; key it by source:id when several mods ask)

.PP
\fB--fomod-defaults\fP[=false]
	answer FOMOD installer questions with the installer's own preselection

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for fill

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	auto-confirm installing the matched mods


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lmm or ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/lmm or ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output JSON instead of text; mutating commands print their result, --dry-run prints the plan; never prompts

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="off"
	diagnostic log level written to stderr (off, error, warn, info, debug)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colored output (NO_COLOR env is also honored)

.PP
\fB--no-hooks\fP[=false]
	disable all hooks

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


